Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.1 field menu panels re-anchored to the 16:9 edges

The field menu and its STSTATUS screens (items, item list, sort, techniques,
status with its digivolve and equipment panels, card folders) keep the PS1
4:3 layout: panels hang from the old left edge (x 0) or right edge (x 320)
and open by scaling from those lines, so in 16:9 their cut ends sit one
gutter inside the picture. With widescreen on, the left column (party pages
and portraits, member cursors, money, EXP, stats, TP, the sort arrows, the
item list's tab) is drawn DW3_MENU_LEFT, one gutter further left, and the
right column (title bars, option panels and their cursors, the status,
digivolve, equipment and technique panels, the help arrow) DW3_MENU_RIGHT,
one gutter further right, with their text windows and scale pivots. The
full-width bands (help bar, item list frame, the chosen item's bar) are drawn
widened by DW3_MENU_BAND: their left parts move left, their right parts
right, and the body tiles fill the middle. The item list's contents stay in
the middle. Only drawing positions change: the shift is applied where the
windows, cursors and sprites are placed, never to the values the menus test.
Off (gutter 0) every position is the PS1 one. The map screen and the
unreachable demo screen are unchanged.

